# Evolve the RE process

Findings alone are not enough. When work **speeds up RE**, **removes a dead end**, or **unlocks a new mod class**, update the living process in the same session.

## Triggers (do this without being asked)

Update process docs/skills when any of these happen:

- A repeatable RE shortcut (search order, Ghidra label, DuckStation watch, script)
- Proof that a prior assumption was wrong (file ownership, VA base, tool limitation)
- A new injectable surface (e.g. `WORLD.BIN`, battle engine, Makou-only path that ships as layers)
- A safer/faster inject or verify path (script replaces manual steps)
- A builder/stack rule players or pack authors must follow

## Where to write

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| End-to-end loop / mental model | `docs/06-new-mod-research.md` |
| Topic reference (encounters, disc, Ghidra…) | matching `docs/0N-*.md` |
| Dated discovery | `docs/findings/` first (`record-findings`) |
| Agent checklist | `.cursor/skills/research-new-mod` and/or `evolve-re-process` |
| New capability unlocked | `docs/06-new-mod-research.md` → **Capabilities unlocked** table |

## Rules of thumb

- Prefer **editing** `06` / `0N` over new meta-docs
- Keep process steps actionable (commands, addresses, “do X before Y”)
- Retire obsolete steps explicitly (strike or delete — don’t leave contradictory guides)
- Commit/push with the finding or ship work (auto-commit applies)

Full checklist: `.cursor/skills/evolve-re-process/SKILL.md`.
